cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use interlingua in research or a publication, please cite it as below."
title: "interlingua: a security-first polyglot message fabric"
abstract: >-
  A canonical, deterministic-CBOR message format signed with ML-DSA-87 and
  sealed with ML-KEM-1024 and AES-256-GCM (the CNSA 2.0 suite), routed between
  labelled trust domains under Bell-LaPadula and Biba rules with a hash-chained
  audit trail, framed as CCSDS Space Packets, with conformance-tested bindings
  for Rust, C, Swift, Go and Java.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: RobS96
version: 0.1.0
license:
  - MIT
  - Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/RobS96/interlingua"
keywords:
  - post-quantum cryptography
  - ML-DSA
  - ML-KEM
  - CNSA 2.0
  - deterministic CBOR
  - interoperability
  - CCSDS
  - information flow control
